    <sys:String x:Key="Help.General.Overview"># [icon:home24] General

The **General** tab is the starting point for every bundle. It holds the application identity, installer, and icon - all deployment targets (Intune, SCCM) share these values.

## Drag and drop

Drop a file onto this tab to get started:

| Input                       | Behavior                                                                                              |
|-----------------------------|-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|
| `.exe` / `.msi` / `.msp`    | Extracts metadata (name, company, version) and icon. New bundle: populates fields. Saved bundle: prompts Apply Full / Upgrade / Extract Icon. |
| `.intunewin`                | Decrypts the package and imports the full bundle. Embedded keys decrypt automatically; otherwise choose vault brute force, manual key, or CSV key list. New/temp workspaces only. |
| `.png` / `.jpg` / `.ico`    | Sets the application icon.                                                                            |
| Folder containing `Config.json` | Opens the existing bundle.                                                                        |

## Fields

| Field       | Purpose                                                                             |
|-------------|-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|
| Company     | Publisher / manufacturer. Flows into folder structure and Intune/SCCM publisher.    |
| Name        | Application display name. Default package name.                                     |
| Dot Version | Dotted notation (e.g. `1.2.3`). Passed as `AppVersion`.                             |
| Version     | Underscore notation (e.g. `1_2_3`). Used in folder paths.                           |
| GUID        | `AppeaseGUID`. Stored in Intune Notes for tracking. Auto-generated.                 |
| Language    | Optional language code (`en-US`, `fr-CA`, etc.).                                    |
| EXE File    | EXE installer filename. Set automatically on drop.                                  |
| MSI File    | MSI/MSP installer filename. Set automatically on drop.                              |
| URL         | Download URL or vendor product page for reference.                                  |
| Icon File   | The application icon used by Intune / SCCM packages, stored as a relative path (e.g. `Icon/AppName.png`). |

## Script framework

Selected when creating a new bundle and *cannot be changed afterwards*. Determines script structure, binary folder, install/uninstall commands, and shortcut files.

- **Appease v2.3** - separate `InstallScript.ps1` / `UninstallScript.ps1` / `DetectScript.ps1`. Installers in `B/`.
- **PSADT v4.1.8** - single `Invoke-AppDeployToolkit.ps1` with Install / Uninstall / Repair phases. Installers in `Files/`.

When importing a `.intunewin` file, the framework is auto-detected from the decrypted content.</sys:String>

