    <sys:String x:Key="Help.General.DetectRunning">Processes that must be stopped before the application can install or uninstall.

## What this section controls

Each row defines a running-process check. At install or uninstall time the packaging engine enumerates running processes; if any row's **Process Name** matches a live process, the deployment can prompt the user, wait, or fail depending on the configured behaviour in the script framework.

## Columns

- **Display Name** - human-readable name shown to end users in prompts (e.g., *Microsoft Excel*).
- **EXE Filename** - installer-side filename, useful when your script needs to correlate a check with a bundled installer.
- **Process Name** - the actual `.exe` name as it appears in Task Manager (e.g., `EXCEL.EXE`). Case-insensitive.

## Toolbar

- [btn:Add] - inserts a new blank row.
- [btn:Remove] - deletes every checked row.

## When to populate this

- The app writes to files that are locked by the running process (Office add-ins, Chrome extensions, background services).
- The installer will otherwise fail with *"file in use"* style errors under SYSTEM context.
- You want Company Portal / Software Center to show a friendly **Close X to continue** prompt instead of a silent failure.</sys:String>

