    <sys:String x:Key="Help.Intune.Installation">Commands and mode for installing and uninstalling the application.

## Commands

Both commands run under SYSTEM context when **Install Experience** is `system`.

**Appease framework - install:**

```powershell
%SystemRoot%\sysnative\WindowsPowerShell\v1.0\powershell.exe -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File Script\InstallScript.ps1
```

**Appease framework - uninstall:**

```powershell
%SystemRoot%\sysnative\WindowsPowerShell\v1.0\powershell.exe -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File Script\UninstallScript.ps1
```

**PSADT framework - install / uninstall:**

```powershell
Invoke-AppDeployToolkit.exe -DeploymentType Install   -DeployMode Silent
Invoke-AppDeployToolkit.exe -DeploymentType Uninstall -DeployMode Silent
```

The uninstall command must cleanly remove the application for Intune compliance reporting. Both fields are required.

## Deployment mode

| Update Mode     | Behavior                                                         | Re-uploads `.intunewin`? |
|-----------------|------------------------------------------------------------------|--------------------------|
| `Create`        | Creates a new Win32 app in Intune.                               | N/A (new)                |
| `Update`        | Updates metadata only on an existing app.                        | No                       |
| `UpdateContent` | Replaces the `.intunewin` content *and* metadata on an existing app. | Yes                      |

- **Existing App ID** - Intune app object ID (GUID). Required when `UpdateMode` is `Update` or `UpdateContent`.
- **Package Option** - optional parameters passed straight through to the `IntuneWin32App` module.</sys:String>

    <sys:String x:Key="Help.Intune.Installation.InstallCommand">Full command line to install the app. Runs under SYSTEM context. Required field.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Help.Intune.Installation.UninstallCommand">Full command line to uninstall the app. Must cleanly remove the application. Required field.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Help.Intune.Installation.UpdateMode">Create: new app. Update: metadata only. UpdateContent: re-upload package + metadata.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Help.Intune.Installation.ExistingAppID">Intune app object ID (GUID) to update. Required for Update/UpdateContent modes.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Help.Intune.Installation.PackageOption">Optional packaging parameters passed to the IntuneWin32App module.</sys:String>

    <sys:String x:Key="Help.Intune.DeploymentBehavior">Controls how the application installs and what happens after installation.

## Install context

| Install Experience | Runs as                          | Typical use                                |
|--------------------|----------------------------------|--------------------------------------------|
| `system`           | SYSTEM (elevated), machine-wide  | Most Win32 apps - **recommended**          |
| `user`             | Logged-in user                   | Per-user installs (e.g. profile-scoped)    |

## Restart behavior

| Value                | Behavior                                                           |
|----------------------|--------------------------------------------------------------------|
| `basedOnReturnCode`  | Respects installer exit codes (`3010` = soft reboot). **Recommended.** |
| `suppress`           | Prevents any restart. May leave the system in an incomplete state. |
| `allow`              | Lets the device restart at its discretion.                         |
| `force`              | Always restarts immediately. Use with caution in production.       |

## Timeouts

**Max Install Time** - minutes (1–1440). Installations exceeding this are marked as failed. Default is `60`. Increase for large applications or slow networks.

## Options

- **Allow Available Uninstall** - lets end users uninstall from Company Portal. Applies only to `available` intent deployments.
- **Featured in Company Portal** - pins the app in the *Featured* banner. Use sparingly.

## Upload

- **Use AzCopy** - uploads the `.intunewin` via AzCopy instead of BITS. Often faster for large packages.
- **AzCopy Window Style** - `Hidden` (silent) or `NoNewWindow` (visible console for diagnostics).</sys:String>

