    <sys:String x:Key="Help.Intune.Assignments">Assignments control how the application is delivered to users and devices.

## Targeting

**Tenant** - which Intune tenants this assignment applies to. Multi-tenant deployments can target several at once.

| Type         | Targets                                      |
|--------------|----------------------------------------------|
| `Group`      | An Azure AD / Entra ID group (by ID or name) |
| `AllUsers`   | All licensed users in the tenant             |
| `AllDevices` | All managed devices                          |

## Group settings

- **Group ID / Name** - GUID for a specific group (single-tenant only), or a group **name** so Wrapp can resolve the matching group per tenant via Graph.

| Group Mode | Effect                                     |
|------------|--------------------------------------------|
| `include`  | App is deployed **to** members of the group    |
| `exclude`  | App is **not** deployed to members of the group |

## Intent

| Intent                         | Behavior                                                           |
|--------------------------------|--------------------------------------------------------------------|
| `available`                    | Appears in Company Portal for self-service install.                |
| `required`                     | Automatically installed on targeted devices.                       |
| `uninstall`                    | Removed from targeted devices.                                     |
| `availableWithoutEnrollment`   | Unenrolled-device install via Company Portal web.                  |

## Notifications

| Notification  | End-user experience                                    |
|---------------|--------------------------------------------------------|
| `showAll`     | Toast notification + Company Portal entry              |
| `showReboot`  | Only notify if a reboot is required                    |
| `hideAll`     | Silent - no user notification                          |

## Scheduling

- **Available Time** - when the app becomes available for installation (ISO 8601).
- **Deadline Time** - when the app must be installed by (`required` intent only).
- **Use Local Time** - when checked, both times use the device's local time zone instead of UTC.

## Restart

| Field                       | Purpose                                             |
|-----------------------------|-----------------------------------------------------|
| Enable Restart Grace Period | Give users time to save work before a required restart. |
| Grace Period                | Minutes before the device restarts after installation. |
| Countdown Display           | Minutes of countdown warning shown to the user.     |
| Snooze                      | Minutes the user can snooze the restart reminder.   |

## Filters

- **Filter Name** - Intune assignment filter for dynamic targeting.
- **Filter Mode** - `Include` or `Exclude` matching devices/users.

## Delivery

| Delivery Optimization | Behavior                                               |
|-----------------------|--------------------------------------------------------|
| `foreground`          | High priority download - fastest, more bandwidth.      |
| `background`          | Downloads in the background - slower, less impact.     |

**Auto Update Superseded Apps** - newer versions automatically replace this app when available.</sys:String>

