    <sys:String x:Key="Help.SCCM.Overview"># [icon:server24] SCCM

The **SCCM** tab defines one or more SCCM (Configuration Manager) application packages that will be created via `New-CMApplication` + `Add-CMDeploymentType` when the bundle runs. Package metadata here layers on top of the shared **General** tab.

## Toolbar

- [btn:Add] - creates a new SCCM package in the current bundle, seeded from the selected template in the **Template** dropdown (or a blank baseline if none selected).
- [btn:Remove] - deletes the currently selected package from the bundle.
- [btn:Duplicate] - creates a copy of the selected package - useful for making a variant (e.g., MSI vs EXE deployment type) without re-entering every setting.
- [btn:Deployments] - opens the deployments editor for the selected package (collections, purpose, schedule). The amber badge counts deployment warnings (incomplete targeting, duplicate collection targets); the red badge counts blocking errors. The same amber/red pair appears on the package list rows and the nav rail, so a problem is traceable from the rail down to the exact field.
- **Template** - selects which preset the [btn:Add] button will use. Templates are created from an existing package via **Save as template** and stored in `%LOCALAPPDATA%\Wrapp\Templates` - no package templates ship built-in, so the list starts empty until you (or an org template pack) save one. A template can also carry the package's **deployments**: check *Deployments* in the save dialog and the dropdown shows a badge with the count - applying such a template replaces the target package's deployments wholesale. `{{Token}}` placeholders expand when the template is applied. Picking a template *after* [btn:Add] does not change the existing package - it only seeds the next one.

## Templates in practice

A typical `MSI Standard` template might set:

```ini
InstallCommand   = msiexec /i "{MSIFile}" /qn /norestart
UninstallCommand = msiexec /x "{MSIFile}" /qn /norestart
DeploymentType   = MSI
InstallBehavior  = InstallForSystem
```

Tokens like `{MSIFile}` are resolved from the General tab when the package is created.

## Target Sites (collapsible)

The collapsible **SCCM Sites** section under the toolbar controls which sites this *specific bundle* is deployed to when it runs. Unchecked sites are skipped. See the info button inside that section for detail on the **Add Site** and **Restore...** controls.</sys:String>

