    <sys:String x:Key="Help.SCCM.SitesPanel">The **SCCM Sites** section controls which sites this bundle is deployed to at run time.

## Site rows

Each row represents one SCCM site with its site **Code**, the **App Folder** where the application will be created, and its **Deployment Groups**. Uncheck a row to skip that site for this bundle only. At least one site must stay selected for the bundle to be processable.

## Add Site

Inserts a blank site row that you can fill in for this bundle. Use this when a site is unique to this package and you don't want to pollute your saved Preferences.

## Restore...

A dropdown that copies sites from another source into this bundle's list. It edits the in-memory bundle only - **Save Bundle** is still required to persist.

- **Overwrite with Preferences** - replaces the bundle's site list with the one saved in Settings &gt; Preferences. Destructive; confirmation is required.
- **Add missing from Preferences** - adds only sites from Preferences whose site code isn't already in the bundle. Non-destructive.
- **Overwrite with App Defaults** - replaces the list with the sites shipped as defaults with Wrapp. Destructive.
- **Add missing from App Defaults** - adds only default sites whose site code isn't already in the bundle. Non-destructive.

**Preferences** are your personal saved site list in Settings. **App Defaults** are the baseline list shipped with Wrapp and never change across updates unless the app itself is updated.</sys:String>

