         ================================================================ -->

    <sys:String x:Key="Help.Inventory.Overview"># [icon:appslist24] Inventory

Browse deployed Win32 applications across your Intune tenants and SCCM sites.

## Toolbar

- [btn:Query] / [btn:Refresh] - loads the app list from Intune or SCCM. The label follows the data state: **Query** for the first fetch of a target, **Refresh** once data is loaded (refreshing clears all caches and re-queries).
- [btn:Filter] - opens advanced filters. The accent pill badge shows how many filters are active.
- [btn:Export] - writes the tenant's entire application inventory to a folder (Intune targets; greyed until the query and its background jobs finish). See **Tenant-wide export** below.
- **Platform toggle** - switches between Intune and SCCM.
- **Tenant / site dropdown** - picks which tenant (Intune) or site (SCCM) to load apps from.

## Getting started

1. Select a platform (Intune or SCCM) using the toggle.
2. Choose a tenant or site from the dropdown.
3. The app list guides you from here: an Intune tenant that needs authentication shows a **sign-in card** (click it - it uses the credentials mapped to that tenant, then queries automatically); an unreachable SCCM site says so; a ready target invites you to click [btn:Query].
4. Click any app to see its full details in the right panel - the faded preview behind the prompt shows the layout the details will fill.

## Background processing

After the app list loads, three background phases run automatically (shown in the status bar):

- **Fetching details** - batch-loads all app metadata. Apps are clickable as soon as this completes.
- **Resolving group names** - resolves Entra ID group GUIDs to display names. Group names update in the detail pane when done.
- **Resolving nested groups** - discovers nested Entra ID group membership for each assignment group.

You can browse apps while background processing runs. The detail pane refreshes automatically when new data becomes available.

The query is tracked in the Background Jobs popup, and its card's **Details** drop-down carries the query statistics - apps returned, assigned vs. not assigned, dependency and supersedence counts - plus, when a query fails, the error code and raw response payload for troubleshooting. Other long-running jobs (bundle copies, downloads) carry their own details the same way (source/destination paths, file counts, sizes).

## Tenant-wide export

**Export** (Intune targets; greyed until the query AND its background jobs finish - the export uses the fully enriched inventory) writes the tenant's entire application inventory to a folder you pick: a `catalog.json` index (app names, ids, versions) at the tenant root, plus a directory per app containing its full detail JSON - with optional nested-group expansions, app icons, and raw `.intunewin` content chosen via checkboxes. The run is a background job with live counters; per-app failures are recorded in the job's details instead of aborting the export. The per-app **Export JSON** action offers the same nested-group option when the app has resolved nested groups - an expansion the Intune console itself doesn't provide.

