## Badge Legend

**Assignment intent:**
- [badge:Required:red] - app is pushed automatically to the target group.
- [badge:Available:blue] - app is offered in Company Portal / Software Center.
- [badge:Uninstall:magenta] - app is removed from the target group.

**Group mode:**
- [badge:+ Include:green] - devices/users in this group receive the assignment.
- [badge:- Exclude:red] - devices/users in this group are excluded.

**SCCM app status:**
- [badge:Enabled:green] - application is active and deployable.
- [badge:Disabled:gray] - application is disabled (won't deploy).
- [badge:Expired:orange] - application has passed its expiry date.
- [badge:Superseded:red] - application has been replaced by a newer version.

## Detail Pane Sections

- **App Information:** name, publisher, version, category, icon, developer, owner, URLs, notes, created/modified dates.
- **Program:** install/uninstall commands, install experience, restart behavior, max install time, content file name and size, return codes.
- **Requirements:** OS version, architecture, disk/memory/CPU requirements, custom requirement rules.
- **Detection Rules:** detection method with expandable script preview for script-based detection.
- **Dependencies** and **Supersedence:** related apps with auto-install/uninstall flags.
- **Assignments:** detailed cards for each assignment (see badge legend above).

## Assignment Cards

Each assignment shows: intent ([badge:Required:red] / [badge:Available:blue] / [badge:Uninstall:magenta]), group mode ([badge:+ Include:green] / [badge:- Exclude:red]), group name, group ID, filter, notifications, availability/deadline dates, restart grace period, delivery optimization, and source.

- Accent-bordered cards indicate a search match - the search query matched this specific assignment's group name, group ID, or nested group.
- **Nested** button appears when nested Entra ID group data is available. Opens a split-panel browser with the group hierarchy on the left and group details on the right.
- Groups showing "(Not Found)" have been deleted from Entra ID but the assignment remains in Intune.

## Actions

- [btn:Refresh] - reloads from Intune/SCCM, clearing all caches.
- **Copy All** - copies all detail sections as formatted text.
- **Export JSON** - saves the full app detail to a JSON file.
- **Import to Wrapp** - creates a new bundle from the app's configuration. Choose *Metadata Only* (fast, config only) or *Full Clone* (downloads encrypted content from Intune).

## Caching

App data is cached per session. Click Refresh to reload from Intune/SCCM. All caches (details, group names, nested groups) are cleared on refresh.

## Search

The search box next to the Refresh button supports structured text search, nested-group-aware matching, and per-assignment highlighting. Because the search surface has its own rich feature set, there's a dedicated help popup - click the info icon beside the search box for the full guide.</sys:String>

    <sys:String x:Key="Help.Inventory.Search">Search across your app inventory. Matching is case-insensitive and supports partial strings.

## What You Can Search

- **App name** -- display name of the application
- **Publisher** -- publisher/manufacturer name
- **Version** -- app version string
- **Group name** -- resolved Entra ID display name of assignment groups
- **Group ID** -- full or partial GUID of assignment groups
- **Nested group names** -- groups nested inside assignment groups, resolved via BFS

## How Matching Works

When you type a search query, each app is checked against:

1. Its display name, publisher, and version.
2. All assignment group names and GUIDs.
3. All nested group names within each assignment group.

If any of these match, the app appears in the filtered list. Nested group search works automatically after the background resolution completes -- no filter toggle is needed.

## Assignment Highlighting

When a search matches an assignment's group name, group ID, or nested group membership, that specific assignment card gets an accent-colored border in the detail pane. This makes it easy to see exactly which assignment caused the match.

Example: searching "Finance" might highlight an assignment whose group "All Finance Users" contains a nested group "Finance-Dept" -- even though the top-level group name doesn't contain "Finance".

## Nested Group Search

Nested group search finds apps where the search term matches a group buried multiple levels deep in the Entra ID group hierarchy. For example, if App A is assigned to "All Employees" and "All Employees" contains "IT Department" which contains "Helpdesk Team", searching "Helpdesk" will find App A.

In the nested group browser dialog, matched group names are highlighted with a left accent bar so you can quickly see where in the hierarchy the match occurred.

## Filters

Use the Filter button for structured filtering by:
- Intent type (Required, Available, Uninstall)
- Assignment presence (has/no assignments)
- Architecture (x64, x86, ARM)
- Minimum OS version
- Content size range
- Relationships (has dependencies, has supersedence)

## Tips

- Partial matches work ("1pass" matches "1Password 8.12.5")
- Group search works after the background processing completes
- Combine search with filters for precise results
- Click the info icon next to the search box to see this help</sys:String>

