    <sys:String x:Key="Help.About.Overview">A desktop app for **Windows application packaging and deployment orchestration** across Microsoft Intune and Microsoft Configuration Manager (SCCM). Takes a single bundle (script framework + installer + metadata + detection + assignments) and lets you build, sign, upload, and assign it across tenants with one click.

## What it accomplishes

- **Unified Win32 packaging** - one bundle, one form-based editor, multiple deployment targets (Intune + SCCM simultaneously).
- **Per-tenant / per-site flexibility** - saved tenants and sites in Preferences seed new bundles; Sync buttons pull updates into existing bundles without rewiring.
- **Safe by default** - all edits are in-memory until Save Bundle; destructive actions (overwrite / reset) confirm first; DPAPI-encrypted secrets; bundle state tracked in a local git repo for time-ordered recovery.
- **Diagnostics included** - inventory browser across tenants, `.intunewin` inspector + decrypter, structured log viewer.

## Core technologies

- **WPF** on **.NET 8** with **CommunityToolkit.Mvvm** for the UI.
- **MSAL** (Microsoft.Identity.Client) for Intune / Entra ID auth; DPAPI for local secret storage.
- **PowerShell SDK** drives the vendored `Wrapp.Packager` module under `modules/` (Intune + SCCM cmdlets).
- **WebView2 + Monaco** for the in-app script / JSON editors.
- **WPF-UI** (Lepo) theme primitives + **MaterialDesignThemes** for the visual language.
- A **purpose-built Markdown renderer** for the themed help popups (what you're reading right now).
- **Git-Windows-Minimal** bundled for per-bundle history without a system git install.

## What's new

Below this text, About shows the recent releases as the same themed **version cards** used by the What's-New popup after an update - one card per version, newest first. The **View all releases** link underneath opens the full release history in your browser (organizations can point the link elsewhere via their defaults file).

